│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ commuting_rz_sharing                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Share each pre/post RZ parameter on the same qubit. The intervening CZ gates commute with │
│                          │ every RZ, so the original block depends only on the sum of each pre/post pair; their      │
│                          │ independent difference is an unobservable flat optimization direction. Using the same     │
│                          │ parameter twice preserves the full reachable effective-angle family while retaining       │
│                          │ strong gradient sensitivity. This reduces parameters per block from 24 to 16 and total    │
│                          │ parameters from 146 to 98 without reducing expressivity, improving parameter efficiency   │
│                          │ and potentially accelerating Adam by removing redundant directions.                       │
