│ patch_description        │ Replace the over-parameterized rotation stack with a QAOA-inspired phase-and-mixer block. │
│                          │ The balanced CZ ring gives every qubit equal entangling degree and is ordered as two      │
│                          │ parallel brickwork layers. A shared RZ retains a trainable collective phase while         │
│                          │ independent terminal RY mixers preserve wire-specific expressivity. Placing the mixers    │
│                          │ last ensures the preceding diagonal feature, CZ, and RZ phases affect the Z readout; in   │
│                          │ the seed's final block, gates after its RY layer commute with the measurement and are     │
│                          │ partly ineffective. Parameter sharing reduces the model from 146 to 56 total parameters,  │
│                          │ which should improve generalization and parameter efficiency while lowering gate count    │
│                          │ and depth.                                                                                │
