│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ hardware_efficient_rx_ry_cnot                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ Replaces the original RY-RZ-CZ-RZ ansatz block with a more parameter-efficient            │
│                          │ hardware-efficient ansatz.                                                                │
│                          │ The new block uses `RX` and `RY` rotations followed by alternating `CNOT` layers to form  │
│                          │ a 1D ring entanglement.                                                                   │
│                          │ This reduces the parameter count per block from 24 to 16, eliminating redundant           │
│                          │ parameters that commute with the final Z measurement (the final `RZ` layer in the         │
│                          │ original code had zero gradient in the last block).                                       │
│                          │ The alternating `CNOT`s also significantly reduce the circuit depth compared to the       │
│                          │ previous linear `CZ` chain. This improves the parameter efficiency of the model and       │
│                          │ reduces the chance of overfitting, aiming to close the generalization gap while           │
│                          │ maintaining high expressivity and training accuracy.                                      │
