│ patch_name               │ antipodal_phase_brickwork                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ This design retains the reliable local RY mixers and ring connectivity seen in the        │
│                          │ strongest candidates, but replaces both the fully collective phase and the                │
│                          │ parameter-heavy independent phase layer with a low-rank antipodal phase field. Four RZ    │
│                          │ parameters are shared across opposite qubits, preserving useful half-turn structure while │
│                          │ allowing substantially more phase resolution than a single collective parameter. Placing  │
│                          │ the mixer before two interleaved CZ matchings ensures that every useful phase field lies  │
│                          │ between population-mixing layers across repeated blocks. The resulting circuit uses 12    │
│                          │ parameters per block (74 total), a compromise intended to recover the lower validation    │
│                          │ loss of the 98-parameter ansatz while retaining stronger parameter efficiency and         │
│                          │ regularization.                                                                           │
