                         Patch Metadata - Gen 12/15 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ rz_even_odd_split_interleave                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the 8 individual RZ parameters with 2 shared groups: even-indexed qubits          │
│                          │ (0,2,4,6) share one RZ parameter and odd-indexed qubits (1,3,5,7) share another. This     │
│                          │ gives 10 unique params per block × 6 blocks = 60 + 2 = 62 total parameters.               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key physics insight: After CZ(even) on pairs (0,1),(2,3),(4,5),(6,7), applying different  │
│                          │ RZ angles to even vs odd qubits creates a differential phase within each entangled pair.  │
│                          │ This is the minimal differentiation needed to break Z-basis commutation while preserving  │
│                          │ the interleaving structure that achieved val_acc=1.00. Within every CZ pair (both even    │
│                          │ and odd layers), the two qubits receive different RZ angles, maximizing expressivity per  │
│                          │ parameter.                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should maintain val_acc=1.00 (unlike the fully-shared 1-param RZ in the 56-param     │
│                          │ design that only got 0.99) while cutting total params by 37% (from 98 to 62), improving   │
│                          │ parameter efficiency and likely convergence speed.                                        │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.3504                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ openrouter/anthropic/claude-opus-4.6                                                      │
│ temperature              │ 1.0                                                                                       │
│ max_output_tokens        │ 16384                                                                                     │
│ reasoning                │ {'effort': 'xhigh'}                                                                       │
│ diff_summary             │ added: 0; deleted: 0; modified: 9;                                                        │
