│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ residual_cross_crz                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The fixed optimizer uses Adam with learning rate 0.03, batches of 15, 30 steps per epoch, │
│                          │ a 0.90 convergence threshold, and validation-loss early stopping with patience 75. These  │
│                          │ settings remain unchanged.                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current block has 24 parameters because it uses independent RZ layers before and      │
│                          │ after an entirely diagonal CZ network. Since RZ and CZ commute, those two RZ layers are   │
│                          │ algebraically redundant. The new block collapses them into one RZ layer while retaining   │
│                          │ all 12 fixed CZ couplings. It then adds four independent, small-angle CRZ residuals on    │
│                          │ the disjoint long-range matching. Because circuit parameters initialize near zero, each   │
│                          │ CZ-plus-CRZ pair starts close to the successful fixed-CZ baseline while allowing Adam to  │
│                          │ tune its effective phase coupling.                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This changes the block from 24 to 20 parameters, reducing the complete model from 146 to  │
│                          │ 122 parameters and the gate count from 300 to 276. The four CRZ gates are parallel and    │
│                          │ replace the depth occupied by the removed RZ layer, so expected depth remains             │
│                          │ approximately 93. The original hypothesis class is retained while the adaptive long-range │
│                          │ couplings can reduce L2 loss and improve convergence.                                     │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.2180                                                                                   │
